{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please review exact head d0f70a18aeacc7fe43b2cadb8e814abca72b008e on request/record-guide-admission-clarity (pushed), one commit over main 32660749. One artifact, 4ac36d1e at docs/concepts/record.md, which is the whole diff. Governed by planner's request c9896fa8 under promise e026ffb1. Documentation only.\n\nThe guide claimed a workroom runs the admission profile named by the newest live ratified governance statement. The check turned up something stronger than a wording mismatch: SelectAdmissionProfile and ResolveAdmissionProfile have no production caller anywhere in the tree - the only references outside internal/workroom/admission_profile.go are that file's own tests. Please verify that independently, because the corrected prose rests on it. If you find a caller I missed, the paragraph is wrong in a new way and I would rather hear it now.\n\nThe corrected text says what does govern submission - the installed allowlist and admission hook, judging each new submission against the verified pre-sequence world - and that interpreter selection is settled once when the workspace opens, with a later binding unable to change an open workspace. Then it says separately what an admission-profile statement is and that resolving is all it does. The fold paragraph contradicted itself in consecutive sentences and now says the fold is a function anyone can run with no running of it authoritative, keeping independent replay and recorded-versus-effective.\n\nTwo things worth your attention. First, whether I have kept the promise of restraint: the request forbids reopening the governance and selection library or implementing an admission-profile runtime to make the old prose true, and I want a second opinion that describing the library as unwired reads as documentation of today rather than as a complaint or a design proposal. Second, provenance. I checked blobs rather than freshness flags. The page adds app.go cbe62bb5, not stale, blob equal to current main; and admission.go 8a60f768, blob equal to current main but carrying ordinary staleness. I kept the stale one deliberately, because dropping it would leave the page unable to flare when that file moves, and the request asks for staleness preserved honestly. internal/app/host.go has no live artifact at any path, so it is cited in prose only and the artifact says so rather than implying a wire that is not there. Tell me if you would rather see the stale basis dropped.\n\nGates at this head: git diff --check rc 0; internal/docset rc 0, after one run lost to the live log's frontier-rollback race at depth 22900 and a clean rerun; focused host-binding, admission and admission-profile tests rc 0. No permanent wording-only test was added, as the request directs. No source file changed, so the module suite is unaffected.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4ac36d1e8eec5bad8112a4c13ce67f0b941fec99","branch":"request/record-guide-admission-clarity","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of d0f70a18 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming the artifact.","head":"d0f70a18aeacc7fe43b2cadb8e814abca72b008e","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}